course: dictionary
lesson: 8657
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. The word season is a good example. Look at the words around it and ask: what is the sentence talking about?
explain: «The year, rik, has four seasons: vesna (spring), lito (summer), osin (autumn) and zyma (winter).» Here the list of spring, summer, autumn and winter tells you that a season is one of the four parts of the year.
explain: «The Okavango river floods in the middle of the dry season.» The word dry tells you this season is a time of year when something happens, here a time with little rain. Mum might say, «Please season the soup with a little salt», and the word soup tells you that season means to add flavour to food.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Season can mean one of the four parts of the year: spring, summer, autumn and winter.
fact: Season can also mean a time when something happens, like the rainy season or the football season.
fact: To season food means to add salt, pepper, herbs or spices to give it flavour.
fact: «The seasons come from the Earth's tilt», so the parts of the year happen because the Earth leans as it goes around the Sun.
fact: In the UK and the USA summer is in the middle of the year, but in Australia and New Zealand the seasons are the other way round.
exercise: In «The seasons are le printemps (spring), l'été (summer), l'automne (autumn) and l'hiver (winter).», what does season mean? | *One of the four parts of the year | A ticket for many games | To add spices to food | A time when something happens
exercise: Mum says, «Season the soup with a little salt and pepper.» What does season mean here? | To cook the soup for a very long time | To pour the soup into a bowl | *To add salt and pepper to give flavour
exercise: «The Okavango river floods in the middle of the dry season.» What does dry season mean? | A shop that sells seasons | A kind of spice | A holiday in the desert | *A time of year when there is little rain
test: What does season mean in «the football season»? | A kind of ticket | To add flavour to food | One of the four parts of the year | *A time of year when something happens
test: In the UK, which season is in the middle of the year? | *Summer | Winter | Autumn | Spring
exam: Jayden says season only means weather. What is the best answer? | Season only means winter | *Season can mean a part of the year, a time when something happens, or adding flavour to food | Season only means a football match | Season is a word for a type of seed
